# Capture-and-resurface (Backlog ritual)

Follows the **`capture-learning`** skill (`~/.cursor/skills/capture-learning/SKILL.md` — read for full conventions). This rule is the always-on reinforcement.

**Backlog files** (active holds `IDEA`/`READY`/`DOING`; archive holds terminal `DONE`/`DROPPED`):
- Per-project: `Backlog.md` / `Backlog-DONE.md` (DMB tooling, corpus threads, refactors).
- Cross-project: `~/.cursor/learnings/Backlog.md` / `Backlog-DONE.md` (AI-tooling, workflow patterns).

When an entry goes terminal, **move the whole block** to the matching `Backlog-DONE.md` in the same write.

**Resurface** before any task that will take **>3 turns or touch >2 files**: skim the active per-project and cross-project `Backlog.md`, match the task against `Surfaces when:` lines in `READY` (and high-confidence `IDEA`) entries, and if 1–3 match, mention inline before starting (`> **From backlog:** *Title* (READY) — reason. Apply, defer, or drop?`). If nothing matches, stay silent — don't surface for tiny tasks.

**Capture proactively** when the user makes a side-aside, tooling wish, or out-of-scope meta-observation: append a block to the right Backlog and acknowledge in one line. `IDEA` when raw, `READY` only when confirmed real work.

**Don't surface during live-play** (dice rolls, die-result lookups, scene narration) — defer to the next planning beat.
